#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:5
#: 940768579b5e49d5b2188e6e76206359
msgid "Dead Reckoning Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:7
#: f86b668b51af498b969eb41db3c16c91
msgid "Copter includes the Dead Reckoning Failsafe that allows a vehicle to return home (or partially return home) if it loses GPS (or more accurately if it loses its position estimate which could be based on GPS, OpticalFlow, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:11
#: f7c42f93c6294b6b998651c6b3e6493e
msgid "This failsafe is available in Copter-4.3 (and higher)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:15
#: 7ca1d17d98d94caebdeb09c4763d4e53
msgid "Similar functionality is available using the `copter-deadreckon-home.lua <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/copter-deadreckon-home.lua>`__ script (`video1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KKShYheW4J0>`__, `video2 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=esM0EqMH_BE>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:18
#: 7c86ff2af5a24c55a00c4b3ae39d3b7c
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:20
#: fcb250ad959e4ecc8be5bc2cacaaaa5f
msgid "Setup :ref:`wind speed estimation <airspeed-estimation>` including setting the :ref:`EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_X <EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_X>`, :ref:`EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_Y <EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_Y>` and :ref:`EK3_DRAG_MCOEF <EK3_DRAG_MCOEF>` parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:21
#: a650810938a04fe5aba6aa40bb197e84
msgid "Set :ref:`FS_DR_ENABLE <FS_DR_ENABLE>` to \"2\" (RTL) or one of the other available options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:22
#: 163dbb3f388d40d2988f252f9a1dc941
msgid "Set :ref:`FS_DR_TIMEOUT <FS_DR_TIMEOUT>` to the number of seconds that the vehicle can maintain control after losing GPS.  On most vehicles this is only 10 to 30 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:25
#: ebac5c7db0674f5b99809e433460c95e
msgid "When will it trigger?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:27
#: 611d5e12cb8b4681a99620972e99428f
msgid "The deadreckoning failsafe will trigger under the same conditions as the :ref:`EKF failsafe <ekf-inav-failsafe>`.  Namely when any two of the EKF \"variances\" for compass, position or velocity are higher than the :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` parameter for 1 second.  In practice it is expected that normally it will be the loss of GPS that will trigger the failsafe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:30
#: 5b053e11a5d04c3ba03fc507b5b6254b
msgid "What will happen when the failsafe triggers?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:32
#: 49c6f519911542648790b216748b7512
msgid "The vehicle will continue to fly normally for 7 to 10 seconds after the loss of GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:33
#: 88ea0da089014d779b3d6d10a9b52b69
msgid "\"Dead Reckoning started\" will be displayed on the GCS and the vehicle will switch to :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` mode and begin flying home"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:34
#: eac6db6f032848b189ec20f616b48e0b
msgid "If the vehicle does not reach home within :ref:`FS_DR_TIMEOUT <FS_DR_TIMEOUT>` seconds, the :ref:`EKF failsafe <ekf-inav-failsafe>` will trigger and the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:35
#: bb4b1117efaa43a699007623cccedb69
msgid "Even if the GPS recovers while the vehicle is returning home, the vehicle will remain in RTL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:38
#: 6c39aa31e8544c98b0846eececd2cc5f
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:40
#: 71e95896dbfc47258b74b14618213ff9
msgid "Follow the instructions below to test in the simulator or on a real vehicle.  If testing on a real vehicle be ready to re-take control in a manul mode (e.g. :ref:`Stabilize <stabilize-mode>` or :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:42
#: 59b2426b312e4564819354e86d862a30
msgid "Set :ref:`RC9_OPTION <RC9_OPTION>` to 65 to allow disabling the GPS from an :ref:`auxiliary switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` (any RC input channel may be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:43
#: 0f24d7e95b9c46e38f2a387a55884b1c
msgid "Arm and fly the vehicle in any mode that requires GPS (e.g. :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>`, :ref:`Guided <ac2_guidedmode>`, :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>`, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:44
#: 29e72adac3e24f7d887083c121e3c313
msgid "Ensure the EKF has calculated a wind speed estimate by checking “wind_dir” and/or “wind_vel” in the ground station (see \"Viewing Windspeed and Direction in Real-Time\" on :ref:`this page <airspeed-estimation>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:45
#: a32465fde83e4c9b9c87655f6e62fcb2
msgid "Raise the auxiliary switch high to disable the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:46
#: c3de602d0f634d22b75a9427404c89e0
msgid "Within 7 to 10 seconds \"Dead Reckoning started\" should be displayed on the GCS and the vehicle should switch to :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` mode and begin flying home"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:47
#: ff35d69ee7fa4412ad42c191ce965a0c
msgid "After :ref:`FS_DR_TIMEOUT <FS_DR_TIMEOUT>` seconds the :ref:`EKF failsafe <ekf-inav-failsafe>` will trigger and the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land mode <land-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:48
#: 44336ffacd12459bb6d5c970f176cda5
msgid "If the vehicle's position drifts too much, switch to :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` mode to recover control of the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:49
#: 1450f2fd4f9b42aab5b04c6029406aaf
msgid "Lower the auxiliary switch at any time to re-enable the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:50
#: 6e5dd64c31cb419e97c86b06e5f65a7a
msgid "Post testing, lower or raise the :ref:`FS_DR_TIMEOUT <FS_DR_TIMEOUT>` parameter to reflect the maximum number of seconds the vehicle can maintain control without GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/deadreckoning-failsafe.rst:53
#: 6a2f819530494330b2017c6edcc3500b
msgid "Videos"
msgstr ""
